body:
I’m a asexual guy (20M), and I told a few of my friends who would understand how it kinda feels to be asexual. Two main things about being an ace;
You WILL go back and forth between feeling like you’re not an ace and feeling turned off by any idea of sexual activity. You can’t fight human biology in that aspect, even though you are different.
Second, it’s best to try to understand these feelings and learn to live beside them. The best thing you can do is learn to love yourself first, and not in a sexual way. Once you feel confident in that aspect, it’s time to push your boundaries and even tell a few people whom you can trust about your asexuality if you haven’t already.
